ALPHAMISSENSE IS NOT REDISTRIBUTED HERE
---------------------------------------

The analysis uses AlphaMissense predictions from

  Cheng J et al. (2023) Accurate proteome-wide missense variant effect
  prediction with AlphaMissense. Science 381:eadg7492.
  doi:10.1126/science.adg7492
  Zenodo record 8208688, doi:10.5281/zenodo.8208688

Those predictions are released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, which is a non-commercial
and share-alike licence. Rather than let those terms travel into this release,
the per-variant columns `am_pathogenicity` and `am_class` have been removed from
every table published here. Everything released is therefore CC BY 4.0 without
exception.

Nothing about the analysis depends on that removal. Run

  scripts/67_restore_alphamissense.py

and the columns are rejoined from the Zenodo record above, on (position,
wild-type, substituted), under the same wild-type residue identity check every
other join in this pipeline carries. The restored values are byte-identical to
the ones the paper was computed from, and tests/test_v2.py then passes in full.

Summary values derived from AlphaMissense do remain: four group medians in
Fig. 2d, two in Fig. 4b, and three rows of results/statistics_final.tsv. Those
are results reported with attribution, not a redistributed dataset.


